WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:01.642
You press Enter.

00:00:01.842 --> 00:00:04.583
Before the page appears, four decisions are

00:00:04.433 --> 00:00:06.637
made about where your request goes.

00:00:06.837 --> 00:00:07.879
Let's follow it.

00:00:08.763 --> 00:00:09.790
First, the name.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.094
Your computer asks a DNS resolver, and gets

00:00:12.944 --> 00:00:15.629
back the addresses of a load balancer.

00:00:15.829 --> 00:00:18.041
That is decision one: which address.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.032
The load balancer is an AWS Network Load

00:00:21.882 --> 00:00:22.739
Balancer.

00:00:22.939 --> 00:00:25.433
It checks the health of every node behind

00:00:25.283 --> 00:00:28.029
it, and sends your request only to a healthy

00:00:27.879 --> 00:00:28.308
one.

00:00:28.508 --> 00:00:29.608
Decision two.

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:33.089
Inside the cluster, the request reaches

00:00:32.939 --> 00:00:35.109
NGINX, the ingress controller.

00:00:35.308 --> 00:00:37.958
It reads the host and the path, and matches

00:00:37.808 --> 00:00:39.279
them to a routing rule.

00:00:39.479 --> 00:00:41.333
Decision three: which Service.

00:00:42.197 --> 00:00:44.131
But a Service is not a program.

00:00:44.331 --> 00:00:46.696
It is a stable name for a set of pods.

00:00:46.896 --> 00:00:49.636
So NGINX looks up the pods behind it, and

00:00:49.486 --> 00:00:50.260
picks one.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.588
Decision four.

00:00:52.464 --> 00:00:55.117
The pod answers, and the response travels

00:00:54.967 --> 00:00:56.221
back the same way.

00:00:56.421 --> 00:00:58.550
One request. Four decisions.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.418
All before the page appears.

